      "text": "To convert the cost of the painting from Namibian dollars to Chinese yuan, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Convert Namibian dollars to US dollars**: \n   We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 7 Namibian dollars. Let \\( N \\) be the number of Namibian dollars it costs. Since \\( N \\) is the given cost of the painting, we start with:\n   \\[\n   N = 105 \\text{ Namibian dollars}\n   \\]\n\n2. **Convert US dollar to Chinese yuan**:\n   We know that 1 US dollar is equivalent to 6 Chinese yuan. Let \\( U \\) be the cost in US dollars. Since \\( U = 1 \\) (since it costs 1 US dollar), we need to find the corresponding value in Chinese yuan.\n   \\[\n   \\text{Chinese yuan} = U \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan per US dollar}\n   \\]\n   Given \\( N = 105 \\) Namibian dollars, we use:\n   \\[\n   N = 7 \\times U\n   \\]\n   Solving for \\( U \\):\n   \\[\n   U = \\frac{N}{7} = 105 / 7 = 15 \\text{ US dollars}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Convert the total amount in US dollars to Chinese yuan**:\n   Now we need to find out how much \\( 15 \\) US dollars is in Chinese yuan. Given \\( 1 \\text{ US dollar} = 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan} \\):\n   \\[\n   \\text{Chinese yuan} = 15 \\times 6 \\text{ Chinese yuan per US dollar} = 90 \\text{ Chinese yuan}\n   \\]\n\nThus, the cost of the painting in Chinese yuan is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{90}\n\\]",
